From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: sky1: keep PERST# deasserted on a warm reboot

The syscore shutdown hook asserts PERST# on every controller, also on a
warm reboot. The PERST# GPIOs are in the always-on S5 domain, so they stay
asserted through the reset, and the firmware's next link training fails for
both RTL8125 ports (LTSSM in Polling.Compliance, 0x40C80) until the board
loses power. Seen 9 of 9 times on warm reboots from this kernel into
Armbian, and never on reboots from Armbian (whose generic host driver does
not touch PERST#).

On SYSTEM_RESTART only disable the controller interrupts and leave the
endpoints alone. Power-off keeps the old behaviour. The boot option
"sky1_pcie_reboot_perst=1" restores it for reboots too, for A/B tests.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1.c
@@ -2461,11 +2461,32 @@ static struct pci_ops sky1_pcie_own_ops = {
 	.write = pci_generic_config_write,
 };
 
+/*
+ * On a warm reboot, leave the endpoints running with PERST# deasserted, as a
+ * kernel without this driver does. Asserting PERST# here leaves it asserted
+ * through the reset (the GPIO is in the always-on S5 domain), and the
+ * firmware's next link training then fails for the RTL8125 ports (LTSSM stuck
+ * in Polling.Compliance) until the board loses power.
+ * "sky1_pcie_reboot_perst=1" restores the old behaviour.
+ */
+static bool sky1_pcie_reboot_perst;
+
+static int __init sky1_pcie_reboot_perst_setup(char *str)
+{
+	return kstrtobool(str, &sky1_pcie_reboot_perst) == 0;
+}
+__setup("sky1_pcie_reboot_perst=", sky1_pcie_reboot_perst_setup);
+
 static int _sky1_pcie_syscore_op_shutdown(struct sky1_pcie *pcie)
 {
 	if (!pcie->is_probe)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART && !sky1_pcie_reboot_perst) {
+		sky1_pcie_disable_irq(pcie);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	sky1_pcie_disable_irq(pcie);
 	sky1_pcie_reset_ep_assert(pcie);
 	if (!pcie->std_pwron)
